    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> Does torch.cuda.synchronize hold the GIL? Ed: I feel like it shouldn't.\r\n\r\nIt does seem to hold the GIL (see the traceback above). I looked through the code as well and didn't spot any place where we are releasing the GIL: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/csrc/cuda/Module.cpp#L444. Unless I'm missing something, it seems like most of `torch._C._cuda` calls don't release GIL.",
