  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@ezyang @wconstab Thanks a lot for helping out with this issue and https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/109159. Although, I suspect this is probably not the last time we will encounter such an issue. We have already hit this issue in 3 separate instances, fixed by these PRs:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/104103\r\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/109454\r\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/109159\r\n\r\nI was wondering if it would be possible to put in a proper long term fix for this issue? One extreme idea I had was to put an assert like `TORCH_ASSERT_NO_GIL_WITHOUT_PYTHON_DEP` before this line : https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/c10/cuda/CUDAException.h#L29 to validate we release GIL always and fix everything that breaks. We could have a test time assert to avoid running this check always and rely on test coverage to catch any issues.",
