  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> but I am definitely amenable to adding this to some critical APIs that you definitely don't want called with GIL.\r\n\r\nThe thing is that we don't really know which API these issues might come from. We are just using high-level torch APIs like `.backward()`, `torch.compile` etc. The issues mostly come from these higher-level APIs calling lower-level APIs which don't release GIL properly. \r\n\r\n> so you would need to have a DEBUG only variant of the assert (and get CI coverage on it)\r\n\r\nI was mostly thinking of something like this so that the check only runs during CI and doesn't impact performance for users.",
