  {
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "I'd like to +1 request for gil tests, it's all too easy to forget to drop the gil somewhere. Note #68739 discussed potential ways but it went nowhere. I'm not sure how expensive running the tests with debug build checking for gil in CUDAException would be, but if that's too expensive, we could maybe LD_PRELOAD `cudaLaunchKernel/cuLaunchKernel` for tests to blow up if gil is held? That would have caught https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/104103\r\nand https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/109454 (the latter if we have autograd tests for multiple output autograd functions)",
